# VERDICT -- the budget condition stays.  Paired at 120 s, gate forced open with
# OGC_DIRGATET=999 against OGC_DIRGATE=0, one replicate each:
#
#                60 s      120 s      120 s off -> on
#   prob_1     -15.5%     +4.2%       492,989 -> 513,703     reverses
#   P27        -15.4%     +6.25%      754,918 -> 802,124     reverses
#   P3          +0.26%    +1.38%    4,514,632 -> 4,577,064   wash at both
#   P33         -9.7%     -3.22%   1,101,010 -> 1,065,571    holds
#   P16        -13.7%     -4.64%   3,199,896 -> 3,051,577    holds
#   P7          -6.9%    +33.80%     695,296 -> 930,323      reverses hard
#
# Two hold at about half their 60 s margin, three reverse, one is a wash.  The rule
# fixed before the run was 4 of 5 agreeing; the count is 2-3.  timelimit <= 60 stays.
#
# Control budget response, which is the clearest structure here:
#   P7 -38.9%, prob_1 -30.0%, P33 -17.3%, P16 -16.7%, P27 -13.7%, P3 -4.6%
# P7 reverses hardest and has the largest control response; P3 barely moves with
# budget and is a wash at both.  But P33 and P16 respond 17% and still hold, so
# "the gate only helps where the control has not converged" does not survive either.
